Part IV — Clinical Validity Oracle

14. The Category Boundary

Formal correctness of software does not imply clinical correctness of the system. The Therac-25 accidents established this precedent. The machine was a system trying to satisfy properties without formally stating them; SAT-MED corrects this by formally stating its properties. But the Therac-25 lesson extends further: AECL did not consider the software design during its assessment of failure modes, asserting the software was free of bugs. Formal specification of software properties does not imply clinical validity of the system.

15. Rule Provenance Schema

Each authorization rule in L4 carries a structured provenance record:

\text{Provenance} = (\text{guideline}, \text{version}, \text{population}, \text{setting}, \text{effect}, \text{CI}, \text{contraindications}).

16. Domain-of-Validity Checker

A formal function

\text{Valid}_{\text{domain}} : \text{Rule} \times \text{PatientContext} \to \{\text{Valid}, \text{OutOfDomain}, \text{Unknown}\}.

If the result is OutOfDomain or Unknown, the rule cannot fire; the system abstains and escalates.

17. Clinical Validity Oracle as Component

The clinical validity oracle is a runtime monitor

\mathcal{V}_{\text{clin}} : \text{RuleSet} \times \text{PatientContext} \times \text{Provenance} \to \{0, 1, \bot_0, \bot_1\}

where the four-valued result distinguishes rule verified, rule violated, inconclusive with no violation found, and inconclusive with violation possible.

The oracle does not verify LTL formulas. It audits the clinical provenance of the authorization rules. Its charter includes:

Oracle separation. No personnel who author authorization rules may sit on the oracle that validates them. The oracle's membership is documented and its independence is auditable.

Disagreement protocol. When clinical professionals disagree on whether a rule's domain of validity applies, the system records a CLINICAL_DISAGREEMENT event and escalates to a designated clinical authority. The resolution is recorded with its provenance.

Oracle compromise. The oracle is a component in the trust model. If the oracle is compromised, the guarantees it provides are retracted. The cross-compromise matrix includes an oracle row and column.

Periodic re-validation. Authorization rules are re-validated at defined intervals against updated guidelines. A rule whose validation has expired is treated as OutOfDomain.

18. Worked Illustrative Calibration

The freshness framework is instantiated for capillary glucose in adult diabetics using the following illustrative parameters: decay function f_\tau(t) = e^{-t/15} (time constant 15 minutes), abstention threshold \theta_\tau = 0.5 corresponding to f_\tau^{-1}(0.5) \approx 10.4 minutes, intrinsic quality \sigma_\tau from the device manufacturer specification, and usage set \mathcal{U}_\tau including insulin dosing (where freshness is critical) and trend monitoring (where freshness is less critical). The calibration is flagged as illustrative and must be replaced by clinician-validated values before deployment.

