Part V — Escalation Automaton with Degraded-Mode Protocol

19. States and Transitions

\mathcal{E} = \{\mathrm{DETECTED}, \mathrm{TRANSPORT\_ACK}, \mathrm{LOCAL\_HUMAN\_ACK}, \mathrm{BACKUP\_CHANNEL}, \mathrm{REMOTE\_CLINICAL\_ACK}, \mathrm{FAILED}, \mathrm{ABSTAINED}\}.

The transition relation is a strict partial order on the first five states, with FAILED and ABSTAINED absorbing:

\to_{\mathcal{E}} = \begin{Bmatrix}
(\mathrm{DETECTED}, \mathrm{TRANSPORT\_ACK}), \\
(\mathrm{DETECTED}, \mathrm{LOCAL\_HUMAN\_ACK}), \\
(\mathrm{DETECTED}, \mathrm{BACKUP\_CHANNEL}), \\
(\mathrm{TRANSPORT\_ACK}, \mathrm{LOCAL\_HUMAN\_ACK}), \\
(\mathrm{TRANSPORT\_ACK}, \mathrm{BACKUP\_CHANNEL}), \\
(\mathrm{LOCAL\_HUMAN\_ACK}, \mathrm{BACKUP\_CHANNEL}), \\
(\mathrm{LOCAL\_HUMAN\_ACK}, \mathrm{REMOTE\_CLINICAL\_ACK}), \\
(\mathrm{BACKUP\_CHANNEL}, \mathrm{REMOTE\_CLINICAL\_ACK}), \\
(\cdot, \mathrm{FAILED}), \\
(\cdot, \mathrm{ABSTAINED})
\end{Bmatrix}

The addition of (\mathrm{DETECTED}, \mathrm{BACKUP\_CHANNEL}) corrects a defect in the original formulation: if a P0 alert's first packet is lost, the automaton must not be forced to wait for a TRANSPORT_ACK before activating the backup channel.

Proposition 19.1 (Direct Jump Forbidden). No transition from DETECTED directly to REMOTE_CLINICAL_ACK exists.

Proposition 19.2 (Transport ACK Not Clinical ACK). TRANSPORT_ACK and REMOTE_CLINICAL_ACK are structurally distinct; no transition equates them.

20. Deadlines and Failure Detection

Each phase q has deadline d(q) = t_0 + \delta(p_{\text{clin}}, q, c). The failure detection is encoded as a clock invariant in the timed automaton (Part II): the automaton may remain in q only while x_q \leq \delta. Violation forces a transition to the next phase or to FAILED.

21. Degraded-Mode Clinical Protocol

Display. The terminal displays a persistent red banner reading "NO ELECTRONIC ESCALATION CHANNEL AVAILABLE — FOLLOW MANUAL PROTOCOL." The display must not simulate normal operation.

Recording. Every FAILED state is recorded with the reason, channels attempted, timestamps, and the identity of the clinician who acknowledged the FAILED state.

Manual escalation. The specification references a clinical companion protocol developed with clinical professionals, defining whom to contact, by what means, and what clinical actions to take while awaiting response. The unfilled state of this protocol is a named stop condition.

System behavior after FAILED. The FAILED state is not silent. The degraded-mode indicator persists until the episode is resolved. The system does not automatically return to normal mode without explicit human confirmation.

