WD full full full full full — full
Oracle full full full full cond full —

Shared dependency row. A shared library or runtime (e.g., a common TLS stack) that spans L2 and L3 is treated as a separate row. If the shared dependency is compromised, the guarantees of both layers are retracted simultaneously, and the matrix entry is "none" for the affected pair.

Critical case. G(L4, L4) is undefined. The only protection is rapid key revocation, external audit, and the watchdog.

30. Failure of Trust Assumptions

If assumption A_k fails, the corresponding guarantee is retracted. The system detects the failure if possible, signals the loss, applies the fallback, and records a TRUST_ASSUMPTION_FAILURE event. If the failure cannot be detected, the guarantee is illusory and the specification documents this limit explicitly. A7 is currently an illusory assumption with a name; the clinical validity oracle is the detection mechanism that makes it non-illusory.

