Q.3 WAL Format and Recovery Algorithm

```
╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
║                     WAL FORMAT AND RECOVERY ALGORITHM                        ║
╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

  WAL RECORD LAYOUT
  ┌────────┬────────┬───────────┬──────────┬──────────────┬──────────────┐
  │ tx_id  │ op     │ payload   │ checksum │ prev_hash    │ signature    │
  │ (u64)  │ (enum) │ (bytes)   │ (H)      │ (H)          │ (S)          │
  └────────┴────────┴───────────┴──────────┴──────────────┴──────────────┘
       │        │
       │        └─ BEGIN | COMMIT | ABORT | MODE_CHANGE | TRUNCATION_LOSS
       └─ unique transaction identifier

  CHECKSUM: H(tx_id || op || payload || prev_hash)
  prev_hash: hash of previous record (hash chain)
  signature: signs (checksum || prev_hash || signer_id)

  RECOVERY ALGORITHM (pseudocode)

  ALGORITHM: recover()
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  INPUT:  WAL (append-only file), last_checkpoint (signed snapshot)
  OUTPUT: mapping from tx_id to {DURABLE, INDETERMINATE, ABORTED}

  1.  state ← {}
  2.  scan WAL from last_checkpoint.offset
  3.  FOR each record r IN WAL:
  4.      IF verify_checksum(r) = FALSE:
  5.          TRUNCATE WAL at r.offset          // record not persisted
  6.          RAISE RecoveryTruncationEvent(r.offset)
  7.          BREAK
  8.      IF verify_chain(r) = FALSE:
  9.          RAISE ChainIntegrityFailure(r.offset)  // stop condition
  10.         ABORT recovery
  11.     SWITCH r.op:
  12.         CASE BEGIN:
  13.             state[r.tx_id].begin ← r
  14.         CASE COMMIT:
  15.             IF state[r.tx_id].begin EXISTS:
  16.                 state[r.tx_id].commit ← r
  17.             ELSE:
  18.                 RAISE LogCorruption(r.tx_id)   // COMMIT without BEGIN
  19.                 state[r.tx_id] ← INDETERMINATE
  20.         CASE ABORT:
  21.             state[r.tx_id] ← ABORTED
  22.         CASE MODE_CHANGE:
  23.             record_mode_change(r)
  24.         CASE TRUNCATION_LOSS:
  25.             record_truncation_loss(r)
  26.  END FOR
  27.  FOR each tx_id IN state:
  28.      IF state[tx_id].begin EXISTS AND state[tx_id].commit EXISTS:
  29.          state[tx_id].final ← DURABLE
  30.      ELSE IF state[tx_id].begin EXISTS:
  31.          state[tx_id].final ← INDETERMINATE
  32.      ELSE IF state[tx_id].abort EXISTS:
  33.          state[tx_id].final ← ABORTED
  34.  RETURN state
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  CRITICAL INVARIANT (recovery_safety_bound, Lean 4):                  │
  │  A transaction whose BEGIN record survived but whose COMMIT is        │
  │  missing or invalid is NEVER classified as Absent.                    │
  │                                                                       │
  │  Rationale: "I do not know" (INDETERMINATE) is a different clinical   │
  │  fact than "it did not happen" (Absent). A clinician acting on the    │
  │  second belief when the first is true may repeat or omit a dose.      │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

